From: fish <lunarisfelix02@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 04:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] op7t-0151: USB Ethernet: drop the send queue on reset, kick it when configured

Three times on 2026-10-26 the phone stopped sending over USB Ethernet some
time after boot while the UI went on: no ARP reply, no live log (udp/5140),
RX 0 packets on the PC; replugging re-enumerated the device but it still
sent nothing. The send queue (32 frames) fills whenever the host stops
reading the bulk IN endpoint (usbipd detached from WSL, cable out); then
ud_if_output drops every new frame without kicking. A bus reset ended the
transfer (tx_busy false) but left the queue full, and ud_configure never
kicked it: the phone could never send again. Now a reset or disconnect
frees the queued frames (logged: "HOTDOGB USB: N queued frames dropped"),
and configuring the endpoints kicks the queue.

Apply after 0150.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
index 843ff0f..522a8ef 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
@@ -449,7 +449,10 @@ ud_configure(void)
 		return;
 	}
 	dwc_wr(DALEPENA, dwc_rd(DALEPENA) | (1u << EP_RX) | (1u << EP_TX) | (1u << EP_INT));
+	lck_mtx_lock(ud.lock);
 	ud.configured = true;
+	ud_tx_kick_locked();                    /* 0151: whatever was queued meanwhile goes now */
+	lck_mtx_unlock(ud.lock);
 	ud_rx_arm();
 	printf("HOTDOGB USB: ECM endpoints configured\n");
 }
@@ -765,10 +768,28 @@ ud_bus_reset(bool rearm, const char *why)
 		}
 	}
 	dwc_wr(DALEPENA, dwc_rd(DALEPENA) & ~((1u << EP_RX) | (1u << EP_TX) | (1u << EP_INT)));
+	/*
+	 * 0151: and the frames queued for the host are dropped. The queue fills whenever the host stops
+	 * reading the IN endpoint (usbipd detached from WSL, cable out): 32 frames, then ud_if_output
+	 * drops every new one and never kicks. A reset ended the transfer (tx_busy false) but left the
+	 * queue full, and ud_configure did not kick it, so after a reset or replug the phone sent
+	 * nothing ever again (2026-10-26, three times: no ARP reply, no live log, RX 0 on the PC) while
+	 * the device itself enumerated fine. Old frames are worth nothing to a new link anyway.
+	 */
 	lck_mtx_lock(ud.lock);
 	ud.configured = false;
 	ud.tx_busy = false;
+	unsigned dropped = ud.txq_count;
+	while (ud.txq_count > 0) {
+		mbuf_freem(ud.txq[ud.txq_head]);
+		ud.txq[ud.txq_head] = NULL;
+		ud.txq_head = (ud.txq_head + 1) % UD_TXQ;
+		ud.txq_count--;
+	}
 	lck_mtx_unlock(ud.lock);
+	if (dropped != 0) {
+		printf("HOTDOGB USB: %u queued frames dropped\n", dropped);
+	}
 	ud.data_alt = 0;
 	if (rearm) {
 		ud_start_setup();
